Details of eks-a cluster installation locally
Requirement - Atleast 16GB ram and 50G storage space

switch to root
mkdir -p WS/EKS; cd WS/EKS


How to install the cluster.
===============================

	Pre-requisite check
	In laptop as the resources are less , few additional things to be taken care. 
		1) Increase the swap if RAM is low (less than 16GB)
                2) edit /etc/sysctl.conf ) and add below entries or modifications to handle the open files/connections

			vm.swappiness=10
			fs.inotify.max_user_watches = 1048576
			fs.inotify.max_user_instances = 512

		3) save the /etc/sysctl.conf and execute below command before installing the cluster

			sudo sysctl -p


Main installation

1) make sure you are in the path where you have mgmt.yaml

if the mgmt.yaml is not present then we have to use (eksctl anywhere generate clusterconfig mgmt --provider docker > mgmt.yaml) to create the file and ensure 1control plane and 1 worker is getting installed as part of cluster creation)

2) nohup eksctl anywhere create cluster -f mgmt.yaml --no-timeouts &

3) to see the king cluster components ( export KUBECONFIG=/root/WS/EKS/mgmt/generated/mgmt.kind.kubeconfig)

4) kubectl get po -A  //this will show you the kind cluster content

Once the cluster installation is completed. Bootstrap (kind) cluster will get deleted and all CAPI, CAPD , EKSA components will move form kind cluster to main cluster. export the KUBECONFIG of main cluster (KUBECONFIG=/root/WS/EKS/mgmt/mgmt-eks-a-cluster.kubeconfig)
to point the reference to main cluster

How to tear down the existing k8s (eks-a) components in laptop
================================================================

1) remove the existing containers. including one which are stopped (docker ps -a). Also do docker system prune.
	also remove the network which is unused (ex: docker network rm kind). Note: host, bridge and none network are created by docker and dont remove them

2) cd /root/WS/EKS

3) make sure you are in the path where mgmt and eksa-cli-logs are present.

4) remove the directories ( \rm -R mgmt eksa-cli-logs)

5) clear nohup.out
